-- sandblaster prelude lemmas: the facts of the ghost prelude's `pow2`, `log2`
-- and `popcount` (elab/ghost.core; §15 S5, SEMANTICS.md §13.10). A
-- hypothesis `0 ≤ n` / `1 ≤ n` is the lemma's second binder.
--
-- Checked, untrusted. Machine-written: each proof is the kernel term the
-- front end produced for the same statement proved in the DSL (induction
-- by `#[decreases(n)]`, `by_unfolding` of the definition, `calc!`), from
-- sandblaster/front/tests/samples/s5_gaps/nat_lemmas/nat.rs;
-- `spec15_s5_gaps::nat_lemmas_match_their_source` checks that the source
-- still proves exactly these statements.
-- Linear arithmetic adds the first four, and `nat::log2_bounds` for
-- `pow2(log2(n))`, to every problem with such an atom (`auto::arith`); the
-- others are applied by name.

